      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://southafrica.co.za/rondebosch.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic Rondebosch Fountain, a Victorian cast‑iron piece, sits on Main Road and marks the suburb's centre.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rondebosch"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Rondebosch Town Hall now houses the Rondebosch Public Library, a landmark that once served as a town hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rondebosch"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Rondebosch was the first permanent title of land founded by Jan van Riebeeck.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://southafrica.co.za/rondebosch.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Rondebosch Common, declared a national monument in 1961, surrounds top‑calibre schools and sports centres.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
